   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization of the\ncounty of Broome to impose an additional one percent of sales and compensating\nuse taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S6228",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6228-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6228\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization\nof the county of Broome to impose an additional one percent of sales and\ncompensating use taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill authorizes Broome County to extend a one percent sales tax for\nan additional two years.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Extends the authorization of Broome County to impose an addi-\ntional one percent sales tax by two years.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nBroome County requested legislation to extend their authorization to\nimpose an additional one percent sales tax, which is set to expire this\nyear.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nExtends Chapter 58 of the laws of 2020.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThis legislation will impose an additional one percent sales tax in\nBroome County, but will have no fiscal implications for the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
